---
const backgroundColor = "rgb(221 185 136)";
const textColor = "rgb(96 65 14)";
const linkColor = "rgb(65 76 48)";
---

<div>
    <h2>Why "Human-First Design"?</h2>
    <p>
        I love technology, but I also love the humans behind it. Behind every great invention, behind every little avatar,
        behind everything great and small, is a human.* And I don't want us to forget that. Therefore, in an age where generative
        AI is making noise to deafen the masses, I want to champion the idea of "human-first design." That is to say, I want to
        preserve the human connection between client and developer. I may use generative AI in making my websites, but everything
        will always receive a human's eye, a human's second opinion. And, if a client is uncomfortable with the idea of gen-AI, I
        don't mind at all building a site with nothing but my two hands! I want clients to remember that there is a human face behind
        all of this. That, even with all the attention on technology, there is still someone out there that cares about her fellow
        humans.
        <br><br>
        Interested in having a website made? <a href="#">Contact me today to discuss details!</a>
        <br><br>
        <span>*For the most part.</span>
    </p>
</div>

<style define:vars={{backgroundColor, textColor, linkColor}}>
    div {
        background-color: var(--backgroundColor);
        float: right;
        width: 80%;
        height: 90%;
        justify-items: center;
    }

    h2 {
        color: var(--textColor);
        font-family: var(--font-kalam), Georgia, serif;
        font-size: 3em;
        text-align: center;
    }
    
    p {
        font-family: var(--font-dm-mono), monospace;
        color: var(--textColor);
        width: 60%;
    }

    span {
        font-size: 0.75em;
    }

    a {
        font-weight: bold;
        color: var(--linkColor);
    }
</style>